  "id": "clinical-practice-guidelines",
  "term": "clinical practice guidelines",
  "definition": "Clinical practice guidelines are systematically developed recommendations for healthcare practice that should be created with clear, rigorous, and transparent methods so their advice is appropriate and reliable. They commonly address clinical management and are expected to be based on systematic reviews while also considering practical context such as costs, feasibility, equity, and acceptability.",
